    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia**_\n\n## Summary\n- `sp-litnotes` now uses `citar-vulpea` only; `citar-denote` is removed. Citation keys live in the `ROAM_REFS` property (`@key`), and `citar-vulpea-mode` is switched on (it was never enabled before).\n- New `sp-litnotes-refs`: `M-x sp-litnotes-refs-report` (dry run, writes nothing) and `M-x sp-litnotes-refs-convert`. It asks up to three questions: move `#+reference:` to `:ROAM_REFS: @key`; create an `:ID:` for notes that have none; add a stub entry to `master.bib` (the inbox) for each key no registered `.bib` has. Every changed note and `master.bib` are backed up first; safe to rerun.\n- The report lists keys that no registered `.bib` has, keys used by several notes, and for each key whether a PDF exists under its own name or only under its `crossref` parent (needed by the DEVONthink link in #209).\n\nFollows #209 (design).\n\n## Test plan\n- [x] 6 ERT tests in Emacs 31.1 batch (`tests/sp-litnotes-refs-test.el`).\n- [x] Dry run read on the real `~/notes/litnotes` (1251 notes): 1185 convert, 1 merge, 65 have no `:ID:` (would get one if you agree), 87 keys are not in any `.bib` (87 stubs for `master.bib`).\n- [ ] Run `M-x sp-litnotes-refs-report` in Emacs, read it, then `M-x sp-litnotes-refs-convert`.\n- [ ] Restart Emacs and check `citar-vulpea` finds the converted notes (`C-c w b n`).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
